  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nA remarkably stagnant and tranquil weather pattern is in store\nfor the foreseeable future. Through the work week the local \narea will be sandwiched between ridging aloft over the central \nU.S. and troughing over the Northeast. This will support general\nsurface high pressure, dry weather and seasonable temperatures.\nRidging aloft is expected to shift east this weekend, keeping \nus dry but likely allowing temperatures to trend a bit warmer. \nHighs mainly in the 60s and lows in the 30s/40s will be the \ngeneral theme. Frost headlines are unchanged early this morning \nwhere the growing season is still active. Given a dry airmass \nwith generally favorable radiational cooling conditions some \nadditional frost is likely at times in coming nights, including \ntonight, particularly across southern/eastern portions of our \narea that typically see the strongest radiational cooling.",
